<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korean debt market closed for Memorial Day.</title>
<headline>S.Korean debt market closed for Memorial Day.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The South Korean debt market was closed on Friday for a national holiday and will open on Saturday, dealers said.</p>
<p>Yields on three-year benchmark corporate bonds closed on Thursday at a new 1997 low of 11.52 percent, buoyed by ample liquidity in the market</p>
<p>* 3-yr corporates close at 11.52 vs 11.65</p>
<p>* 3-mth CDs end at 11.70 vs 11.95</p>
<p>* Overnight average call rates at 11.10 vs 11.32</p>
<p>-- Yeom Yoon-jeong (822) 727 5647</p>
